    {
      "id": "claim_336105228c7a4f48870a324b7f5b4f73",
      "statement": "sendZeroHubMessage throws when isDisconnected is true, when no WebSocket exists, or when the socket exists but its readyState is not OPEN (a CONNECTING or CLOSING socket) — without that last guard ws.send() would throw a raw InvalidStateError that could escape the calling event handler. A disconnected client must reconnect via a hub entry point (createRandomHub, joinRandomHub, joinStaticHub, or joinOrCreateIPHub) before sending.",
