    {
      "id": "claim_0bb2463bfe094c7db8b7ead9edcf6878",
      "statement": "When every configured host's same-host retry budget is spent on every allowed sweep (including the single-configured-host case, where wraparound to itself is not a new host), reconnect() sets the reconnectAbandoned latch and surfaces the terminal failure ALL_HOSTS_EXHAUSTED_ERROR_MESSAGE ('all ZeroHub hosts are not working, please check the ZeroHub hosts') via reportZeroHubError/onZeroHubError; no further automatic retry is attempted, and the latch is cleared only by a fresh entry-point call.",
