    {
      "id": "claim_bb5769354e864cb2bc46833d98cc362e",
      "statement": "Peer creation and teardown are centralised in the shared addPeer and removePeer helpers: addPeer builds a Peer with a fresh RTCPeerConnection, parses metadata, wires the connection and ICE state handlers, stores it, and marks it Pending; removePeer clears the peer's pending ICE-candidate and P2P-drop recovery timers, closes the RTCPeerConnection, nulls the state handlers so a stale ICE event cannot call restartIce on a closing connection, and deletes the peer from the map (a no-op if already gone). These are shared by the hubInfoMessage, peerJoinedMessage, peerDisconnectedMessage, roster-prune, and disconnect paths so teardown semantics cannot diverge.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L1122-L1154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:65f365d707c7fbe18363aa28f529f6b2a399024717b13fc47609658a5ad95af9:"
