    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fe80df61090748b8992b0111552683e8",
      "statement": "On a 1001 migration redirect, reconnect first validates the close reason with isWellFormedHost (a bare hostname or host:port with no scheme, path, userinfo, whitespace, or port > 65535, mirroring the server's validateBackupHost and deliberately accepting non-canonical-but-valid spellings such as uppercase hosts and zero-padded ports); a malformed reason (e.g. a proxy's 'Server going away' text) falls back to the automatic host-failover path without touching host state, and a reason equal to the current host is rejected through onZeroHubError instead of retrying. On a valid redirect the client updates this.host to the redirect target and, when the target is in the configured hosts list, points hostIndex at its position, so later entry points and failover start from the redirected host rather than the stale one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/utils.ts#L51-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b42185d8f66f226f899c5e67177fc31146534146875516ff50408cabeb73f80a:"
