    {
      "id": "claim_ea59de1b8139452d86d9932f2f146675",
      "statement": "With autoAnswer: false, the offerMessage branch does not call sendAnswer; it moves the peer to AnswerPending and then invokes the public onOffer(peer, offerSdp) callback (guarded on the peer existing in the peers map) so the application completes the exchange via sendAnswer(peer.id, offerSdp). With autoAcceptAnswer: false, the answerMessage branch likewise moves the peer to AcceptPending and invokes the public onAnswer(peer, answerSdp) callback so the application completes the exchange via acceptAnswer(peer.id, answerSdp).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L832-L871",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a9581ddf9f58fdffacd118a1f9c5c870c65ea8f10f1b24f5dc0640e4559e4a6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_229a309d921a4176b3233d02a2dac5c5",
      "statement": "ZeroHubClient exposes two public callbacks for manual SDP handling: onOffer(peer, offerSdp) is invoked when an offerMessage arrives while autoAnswer is false (the peer has just transitioned to AnswerPending) instead of being silently dropped, so the application completes the exchange by calling sendAnswer(peer.id, offerSdp); onAnswer(peer, answerSdp) is invoked when an answerMessage arrives while autoAcceptAnswer is false (the peer has just transitioned to AcceptPending), so the application completes the exchange by calling acceptAnswer(peer.id, answerSdp). Both callbacks are guarded on the peer still existing in this.peers, so a dangling offer/answer for a peer already torn down is not surfaced.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L250-L264",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dcdeb950e92cdb991ae5eb0fd3970da02acf1ca13e0c0783b2b4393a28ed51a6:"
        },
